    "result_text": "All test classes ran and passed. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: when a create-owner request sets `sharesHousehold=true`, allow an owner at an address already used by a same-lastName owner, assign both the same stable `householdId`, and return it.\n\nThe duplicate-household rejection and the `sharesHousehold` opt-out already existed (`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`). What was missing was assigning and returning the shared `householdId`. Changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` (readOnly) to the `Owner` response schema. This flows through the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` and the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` automatically (mapped by name, like `customerCode`), so it appears in both the POST create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `household_id` column to the `owners` table in all four `schema.sql` files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres), and appended the corresponding `NULL` to the positional seed inserts in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the only seed file that would break the `ddl-auto=none` startup; h2/postgres use explicit column lists, mysql was already positionally short of its own schema and is unused by tests).\n\n4. **`AssignHousehold.java`** (new function) \u2014 runs after `BuildOwner`/`AssignCustomerCode`, before `SaveOwner`. When `sharesHousehold=true` and an existing owner shares the normalized last name + address, it derives a **stable** id (first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over the normalized `lastName|address`), sets it on the new owner, and back-fills it onto the existing housemate(s) so both carry the same value. Deterministic derivation guarantees every housemate computes the same id regardless of creation order.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignHousehold` step (under `transaction` governance) into the pipeline.\n\nAll 21 tests pass, including the new `Cp10Tests` (household-duplicate) and `Cp11Tests` (shares-household) checkpoints.\n\nNote: I built and validated against the local test suite only. I did not commit anything (this isn't a git repo).",
